{
  "_comment": "HOOK MODE: no arguments, payload read from STDIN. This is a HARDENING, not a bug fix, and the distinction is recorded because an earlier commit message of mine got it wrong. The previous registration passed -Route with the CLAUDE_USER_PROMPT placeholder and it WORKED: measured against commit 59b2620 in a real marketplace install, three prompts routed to FORGE, EMPATHIC and CLINICAL correctly. The claim that it shipped dead came from misreading the harness debug log -- the line reads \"Hook UserPromptSubmit (UserPromptSubmit) success:\" and the hook output is printed on the NEXT line, so grepping only the matching line shows nothing. Hook mode is kept anyway for two measured reasons: it depends on no harness-provided variable, and an empty route makes the ps1 wait on stdin forever (exit 124), which is a real latent hang; and it stops PreToolUse from passing a FABRICATED all-zero gauge vector. Measured: 5 of 5 sessions emit the marker and the lane varies with the prompt.",
  "_comment_coverage": "EVERY EVENT THE CLI DEFINES, WILDCARD MATCHER -- 2026-08-08. This manifest covered THREE events, then ELEVEN, and now THIRTY-ONE. The jump from eleven to thirty-one came from the Socio asking a question I could not answer: is there a SubagentStart, and are eleven really all of them? There is, and they are not. The eleven were derived by COUNTING WHICH EVENTS OTHER INSTALLED PLUGINS USED -- a lower bound that can never reveal an event nobody on this machine happens to use, which is precisely how SubagentStart was missed. The thirty-one below come from the authoritative source instead: the Lz array inside the compiled claude CLI binary, cross-checked against its execute<Name>Hooks dispatch functions, and listed here in the CLI's own order. TaskStop was found nearby and deliberately EXCLUDED -- its surrounding text reads 'use TaskStop with task_id', so it is a tool, not an event. Tolerance was measured BEFORE the wiring was written, as it was for the eleven: all four hook arms were fired with each of the twenty new event payloads on stdin, 80 invocations, 0 non-zero exits. A hook that crashed on ConfigChange would break every session it fired in. The wildcard matcher is likewise measured: an installed plugin registers Stop with matcher \"*\", so \"*\" is accepted on events that carry no tool name.",
